WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.520
A starburst cell has branches pointing every way.

2
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.500
Which ones inhibit a given ganglion cell?

3
00:00:10.483 --> 00:00:16.983
In 2002, Euler, Detwiler and Denk imaged calcium in single starburst dendrites, in

4
00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:17.983
rabbit retina.

5
00:00:18.683 --> 00:00:23.623
A dendrite gave larger calcium signals for motion outward from the cell body than

6
00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:24.623
for motion inward.

7
00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:29.437
Predict. The cell body sits where all the branches meet.

8
00:00:30.337 --> 00:00:31.417
What should its voltage show?

9
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.500
Little preference.

10
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.760
Motion outward along one branch runs inward along the branch opposite it.

11
00:00:44.633 --> 00:00:47.993
A soma that simply summed equal spokes would see them cancel.

12
00:00:48.873 --> 00:00:52.293
The measured somatic voltage did not show the dendrites' preference.

13
00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:55.447
So the branch, not the cell, is the unit.

14
00:00:56.347 --> 00:00:59.767
Each branch has its own preferred direction, set by where it points.

15
00:01:00.817 --> 00:01:05.057
One limit here. A calcium signal is not transmitter release.

16
00:01:08.117 --> 00:01:12.997
In that simple sum, input taken equally from every branch carries no direction

17
00:01:12.997 --> 00:01:15.737
signal. So the wiring should be selective.

18
00:01:16.817 --> 00:01:19.137
Paired recordings in rabbit had shown it.

19
00:01:19.917 --> 00:01:23.997
Branches pointing in a ganglion cell's null direction inhibited it, and

20
00:01:23.997 --> 00:01:25.697
preferred-pointing branches did not.

21
00:01:26.717 --> 00:01:32.617
In 2011, Briggman, Helmstaedter and Denk read the wiring directly, in mouse retina.

22
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:38.920
First they imaged calcium during moving bars, to find each ganglion cell's preferred

23
00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:39.920
direction.

24
00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:45.400
Then they cut the same tissue for electron microscopy, and traced the cells and

25
00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:46.400
their contacts.

26
00:01:47.883 --> 00:01:51.583
Predict. Take a cell that prefers rightward motion.

27
00:01:52.483 --> 00:01:54.423
Which way should its contacting branches point?

28
00:02:00.433 --> 00:02:04.813
Most starburst input came from branches pointing roughly left, in the null

29
00:02:04.813 --> 00:02:05.813
direction.

30
00:02:06.317 --> 00:02:11.157
And the direction of the individual branch predicted contact better than the line

31
00:02:11.157 --> 00:02:12.177
between cell bodies.

32
00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:19.710
One limit. A contact shows wiring, not synaptic strength.

33
00:02:20.733 --> 00:02:22.033
So the picture holds.

34
00:02:22.893 --> 00:02:27.253
Most starburst contacts come from branches pointing roughly in the cell's null

35
00:02:27.253 --> 00:02:27.653
direction.
